{
  "headline": "Crude down 3% to $98.41 on Trump-Putin diesel deal; grains flat",
  "lead": "Crude fell about $3 overnight to **$98.41** on word of a US-Russia deal that could add diesel supply. Corn at **$4.73** and beans at **$12.61** barely noticed. For harvest fuel bills, that is the first bit of relief in a while, though crude is still close to $100.",
  "teaser": "Crude slips 3% on a diesel supply deal while corn and beans hold flat at the start of the week.",
  "one_number": {
    "value": "$15.4 billion",
    "unit": "India's September crude import bill",
    "context": "That is up 46% from a year ago, from $10.5 billion."
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Crude slips on diesel deal",
      "body": "- WTI is at **$98.41** overnight, down 3.0%, after the Trump-Putin diesel agreement raised hopes for more supply.\n- The dip starts from a high level, and record freight costs are already forcing oil sellers to cut prices.",
      "so_what": "Diesel supply is the harvest-season input story right now.",
      "conviction_level": "medium",
      "overnight_surprise": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Grains hold flat",
      "body": "- Corn is at **$4.73** overnight, down 1¼ cents, and beans are at $12.61, down a quarter of a cent.\n- Feedstuffs says grains are still struggling for momentum after the WASDE, with harvest pressure feeding the bears and demand signals mixed.",
      "so_what": "No news to move them, so harvest supply is setting the pace.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Cattle edged up Friday",
      "body": "- Live cattle settled Friday at **$227.55**, up 0.7%, and feeders settled at $343.625, up 0.1%.\n- Feeders say prices have dropped since packing plant closures, so cash trade is the thing to watch.",
      "so_what": "Packer capacity is limiting how far cattle can run.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": false
    }
  ],
